  <Data version="2" dbID="0">
    <Name>*Wood</Name>
    <Info>softwood Because of their swelling and shrinking, the material data of wood materials depend on their present and past moisture content. The applicability of WUFI has to be judged case by case.

Hardwood, softwood: these material data are primarily meant for the calculation of diffusion processes. To be used in cases without capillary water uptake by the wood, e.g. drying out of roof boards etc.

Oak / spruce radial / longitudinal: the liquid transport coefficients have been determined from the moisture behaviour of specimens exposed to natural weather. The moisture-dependence of the mu-value is already included in the liquid transport coefficients. 
Dww=Dws because of swelling phenomena. Great dependence on swelling condition! To be used for wooden parts in direct contact with rain water (e.g. framework constructions), but with caution and only for estimative calculations.</Info>
    <Flags>12</Flags>
    <Type>0</Type>
    <Color>$80FF</Color>
    <NoMoistureTransport>TRUE</NoMoistureTransport>
